# Format preview locks

LOTAGENT has three layout formats. The local `next dev` Format bar (iPhone / iPad / Desktop) picks which one you are editing.

| Selected | True size | Edit file | Scope |
|----------|-----------|-----------|--------|
| **iPhone** | 390×844 | `src/app/format/iphone.css` | That device only |
| **iPad** | 834×1194 | `src/app/format/ipad.css` | That device only |
| **Desktop** | full window | `src/app/format/desktop.css` | **All devices** (shared source of truth) |

## Rules

1. If Format is **iPhone**, change only iPhone. Put CSS in `iphone.css` inside `@container la (max-width: 560px)`. Do not edit `ipad.css` or `desktop.css`.
2. If Format is **iPad**, change only iPad. Put CSS in `ipad.css` inside `@container la (min-width: 561px) and (max-width: 960px)`. Do not edit `iphone.css` or `desktop.css`.
3. If Format is **Desktop**, put shared layout in `desktop.css`. Those styles apply on every device unless iPhone or iPad files override them. Do not add iPhone-only or iPad-only hacks in `desktop.css`.
4. Do **not** add format-specific layout to `src/app/globals.css`. Shared tokens and colors stay there.
5. `html[data-la-format]` / `.phone-sim` / `.tablet-sim` / `src/app/format/shell.css` are **device chrome only** (bezel, studio bar, scroll lock). Not product layout.
6. Real phones and iPads use the same `@container la` queries, so preview edits ship as the real responsive version.

The Format bar is development-only. It never ships to Vercel.
